{
  "name": "arm-link-driven",
  "description": "The arm link as Fusion would set it up: the shoulder turns on a pin (its bearing) and is driven through four M3 holes of a servo horn on a 27mm circle, which is what actually holds it against the payload. The wrist bearing takes the payload as a bearing load (a shaft pushing on one side of the bore) plus the wrist motor's 1.5 N\u00b7m reaction torque; a side case adds a lateral push. The link carries its own weight.",
